@startuml
title SysMon - User Deletion Sequence Diagram

participant "SysMon Frontend" as Frontend
participant "SysMon Authentication System" as Auth

note over Frontend
  Admin (Tier 1) opens the Users panel, selects Manage Access,
  selects an existing user and selects Delete User.
  The Frontend displays the deletion confirmation panel.
end note

alt Admin confirms deletion
  Frontend -> Auth : POST /v1/users/{userId}/deletion\nAuthorization: Bearer token\n{adminPassword}
  Auth -> Auth : Validate token

  alt Token missing, invalid or expired
    Auth --> Frontend : 401 Unauthorized\n{code, message}
  else Caller is not a Tier 1 admin
    Auth --> Frontend : 403 Forbidden\n{code, message}
  else Admin password missing or incorrect
    Auth --> Frontend : 403 Forbidden\n{code, message}
  else User does not exist
    Auth --> Frontend : 404 Not Found\n{code, message}
  else Own account or last Tier 1 admin
    Auth --> Frontend : 409 Conflict\n{code, message}
  else All checks passed
    Auth -> Auth : Delete selected user account
    Auth --> Frontend : 204 No Content
  end
else Admin cancels deletion
  note over Frontend, Auth : No request is sent. The user account is left unchanged.
end

@enduml
